==Strategy==
To deal with this stage you will want to bring a lot of spammable units, since Daboo, or the peons themselves, will likely wipe out most Ubers in just a few attacks. Holy Blast is likely the best choice of [[Cat Cannon]] by far here, as it can take huge chunks off Daboo's health with each use, and if at level 20 or above, can oneshot Daboo's corpse if he wasn't Z-killed.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]: A great unit here, as they're pretty spammable, and also have a long, high-damaging Wave Attack that can clear almost the whole field.
*[[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]]: An extremely spammable attacker with great stats, especially against the Brollows.
*[[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]]/[[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]]: Anti-Angel attackers that can both devastate the Gabriel waves. Cafeteria Cat has enough damage to 1-shot a Gabriel, but Mushroom Cat can attack multiple at once.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Has great stats against the Wild Doges, and can even be used for other peon waves, however, using them against the Brollows is a really bad idea, as Courier will make them rebound a lot.
*[[Ancient Egg: N112 (Rare Cat)|Cat Egg Pod]]: Makes the Wild Doge waves significantly easier, as at level 50, they can 1-shot a Wild Doge, on top of their ridiculous defense against them with their Dodge.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]]: Has rapid attacks with high damage that can easily eradicate peons. Plus, he has great health to survive a bunch of attacks from Daboo and a quick recharge.
*[[Lasvoss (Uber Rare Cat)|Lasvoss Reborn]]: Has immunity to Daboo's slow, and can deal ridiculous levels of damage against the enemies. He has a somewhat slow attack rate, and his recharge isn't quite as fast as Balrog's, but he still works here.
*[[Baby Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Cats in the Cradle]]: With devastating high-damage Wave Attacks, they can clear out peons effortlessly while also having the health to tank a few attacks. Their Ultra Form makes them much less likely to miss an attack as well.

==Trivia==
*Drowsy Paths's Japanese name, Kokkuri Sanpodō, is a pun on [[wikipedia:Kokkuri|Kokkuri-san]], a Japanese game used in divination similarly to how one would use an Ouija board. ''Sanpodō'' means "promenade".

